WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:04.604
-And now here he is,
Jimmy Fallon!

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.373
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.242
♪ -Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.011
♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.845
♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪
-What?!

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.280
♪ -Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.083
-Wow!
♪ -Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.417
-Wow!

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.887
♪ -Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:29.028
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.097
-Oh, my goodness. Wow!

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.298
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.067
Is it real? Oh, my gosh!

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.470
Is this really happening?!

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.505
Thank you very much!

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.173
Please, please, please.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.909
Thank you very much.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.546
Wow. Welcome, welcome,
welcome, everybody,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.082
to "The Tonight Show!"
You guys, we are --

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:53.085
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:56.623
We are finally back home
in Studio 6B.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:01:00.460
It is so good...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.763
...to see this beautiful set
and this crowd right here.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:09.202
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.905
And also the family of raccoons
that now live in my desk,

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:15.074
which is --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.743
Please, just give me a minute
to soak up this audience.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.846
I've never been
so excited to do a show

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.847
for 58 people in my entire life.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.116
This is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:29.689
This is what -- this is --
this is -- seriously!

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:36.696
Seriously, after --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.232
After last year,
this is like performing

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.833
at a sold-out
Madison Square Garden.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.002
It really feels that way.
It really does.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.938
That's right. For the first time
in over a year,

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:47.774
we have an actual crowd.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.210
So now if you hear total silence
after a joke,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.744
that's just because
it wasn't good.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.912
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.914
Yep, all week, our audience
will include

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.116
first responders
and healthcare workers.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:04.757
-Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.794
-Everyone here is fully masked,
fully vaccinated,

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.528
and fully skipping work,
by the way.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.464
[ Laughter ]
You deserve it.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.499
Of course, I just want to thank
all of you for everything

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.535
you've done for this country
in the past year.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:22.441
Thank you very much.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.278
Alright, everybody, let's start
the show with some fun news.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:28.881
March Madness is in full swing,
and we're down to the Sweet 16.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.684
And already, there are
zero perfect brackets left.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.985
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:35.054
Yeah, I can't believe
our strategy of five minutes

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.223
of research and blind guessing
didn't work.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.591
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.093
Those are one of the jokes
that didn't work, guys.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.327
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.729
You'll be hearing them
throughout the evening.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.798
-It's real, man. It's real.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.600
-One of the biggest upsets
was number 8 Loyola Chicago

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.036
knocking off number 1 Illinois.

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:54.540 line:0%
And no one's happier about it
than 101-year-old nun

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.909 line:0%
and team chaplain Sister Jean.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.080 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.582
She was psyched.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.317
After the game,
Sister Jean was amped up.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.085
In the locker room,
she was spraying holy water

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.421
like it was champagne.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.256
And during the broadcast,
they talked about Sister Jean's

00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:13.359
pregame prayer that she
delivered to the team.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.028
It's amazing. Listen to this.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.595
-Here's what she told them.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.499
"As we play the Fighting Illini,
we ask for special help

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.034
to overcome this team
and get a great win.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.703
We hope to score early
and make our opponents nervous.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:27.774
We have great opportunity
to convert rebounds as this team

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:31.678
makes about 50% of layups
and 30% of its 3-pointers.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.613
Our defense can
take care of that."

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.680
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.150
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.551
-Right now,
Charles Barkley is like,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.720
"She's better at analyzing
college basketball than I am!"

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.355
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.956
If you think that's shocking,
next season,

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.793
Sister Jean is being added to
the cast of "Basketball Wives."

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.195
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.564
Meanwhile, the tournament's
true Cinderella

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.699 line:0%
is Oral Roberts University.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.568 line:0%
They beat Ohio State
and Florida,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:59.872 line:0%
becoming just the second 15 seed
in history to make the Sweet 16.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.708
Oral Roberts fans were like,

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.843
"Maybe now people will stop
thinking we're a toothpaste."

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.711
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.813
Actually, "Oral Roberts" sounds
like something

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:09.382
you can't say around
Sister Jean.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:13.018
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:16.856
After Oral Roberts pulled off
their second huge upset,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.358
the students back on campus
in Tulsa were pretty excited.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.392
Take a look at this.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:26.699
[ Cheering ]
-Enjoy it. Soak it in.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.868
-Even spring breakers in Florida
were like,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.737
"Everyone's pretty close.
Just saying."

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.772
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:35.541
Yeah, not only is it
March Madness,

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.243
it's also spring break season.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:40.079
But over the weekend, Miami
declared a state of emergency

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:43.082
and mandated a curfew
due to COVID concerns.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.550
You know things
are out of control

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.285
when Florida
is worried about COVID.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:50.289
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.192
College kids were like, "It's
a shame, 'cause I flew to Miami

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.695
during a pandemic
to party very responsibly."

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.463
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.566
Yep, now there's a curfew
from 8:00 p.m. to 6:00 a.m.,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.802
so spring breakers will have to
return to their motel rooms.

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.671
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.173
The best way
to guard against COVID

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.275
is forcing drunks
into small, confined spaces.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.877
That's what I've always heard.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:12.911
Some more news here.

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:14.247
Just when you thought
he was gone,

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.482
I saw that former
President Trump is creating

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.717
his own social-media platform.

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.519
If it goes according to plan,

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.587
it'll be the first thing
he'll help go viral

00:05:22.587 --> 00:05:23.823
since the coronavirus.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.324
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:31.063
[ Applause ]

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:34.967
But you have to be careful with
the Trump social-media platform.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.502
The site will automatically flag

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.604
any statements
that turn out to be factual.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.139
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:43.309
Meanwhile, not to be outdone,
last week, Joe Biden joined

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.044
Tumblr on the stairs
of Air Force One.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.880
Take a look at --
Whoop! There you go.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.116
Oh, boy! Whoa!

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:52.852
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.087
At that point, just lay there.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.256
"I'm taking my Zoom meetings
from here."

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.658
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:01.093
Speaking of Trump,
I just saw an update on

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:03.162
what's going on
with his old private plane.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.530
Watch this.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.398 line:0%
-It was the ultimate
status symbol --

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:08.767 line:0%
Donald Trump's Boeing 757.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:11.703 line:0%
Today, however, the massive jet
sits abandoned

00:06:11.703 --> 00:06:13.705 line:0%
at an upstate New York airport.

00:06:13.705 --> 00:06:15.374 line:0%
One engine mostly missing,

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:18.310 line:0%
one wrapped, idle,
in apparent disrepair.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.847 line:0%
According to records,
it hasn't been flown in months.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:24.817
-Yeah, one engine wrapped,
the other's missing.

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.552
Or as United put it,
"We'll take it!"

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.686
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:30.456
"Get that baby in the sky!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:33.158
Some business news --
I saw that Krispy Kreme is

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:36.896
giving free glazed doughnuts
to customers who get vaccinated.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.497
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.199
I'd like to meet
the one person who's like,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.901
"I wasn't gonna
get the vaccine, but...

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.703
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.339
"...I heard about
that free doughnut."

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.941
[ Applause ]

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.010
"You pick the arm. I don't care.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.379
I hold a doughnut with this arm.
So you gotta get --"

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.181
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:59.252
So if obesity wasn't your
pre-existing condition before...

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.953
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.388
...it's about to be.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.923
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.958
I heard about a winery
in California

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.492
that's offering
a pretty sweet job.

00:07:07.492 --> 00:07:08.661
Listen to this thing.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.363
-The Murphy-Goode Winery
in Sonoma, California,

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:16.268
is offering $10,000 a month to
work and live there rent free.

00:07:16.268 --> 00:07:18.470
The company is looking for
someone who

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.173
"takes life one sip at a time."

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:22.474
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:24.377
-When they heard that,
every parent trying to

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.145
teach their kids on Zoom
was like...

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.746
[ Cheering ]

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:30.316
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.150
Check this out.
A man in California is

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:37.489 line:0%
being investigated for
using a drone to deliver meth.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:40.659
Police got suspicious when they
saw the man 200 feet in the air,

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:41.928
hanging onto the drone.

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:45.197
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:47.800
And finally, a United flight
from Newark to Miami

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.303
was diverted after one man
bit another passenger's ear.

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:52.537
[ Audience oohs ]

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:54.239
When United heard,
they immediately charged him

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:55.908
$8 for an in-flight snack.

